# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FPL Draft Co-Pilot — environment reference
# Copy to .env at the repo root. Both Go binaries and the Python CLIs load it
# automatically (a real exported environment variable always wins).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Core: these three are all you need ───────────────────────────────────────

# Your FPL Draft league id — in the URL on draft.premierleague.com
# (e.g. /league/12345/... -> LEAGUE_ID=12345).
LEAGUE_ID=your-league-id

# Your entry (team) id — in the URL when viewing your team
# (e.g. /entry/67890/... -> ENTRY_ID=67890).
ENTRY_ID=your-entry-id

# A password YOU invent (nobody issues it) so only your own Claude clients can
# call the MCP server. Generate one:  openssl rand -hex 16
FPL_MCP_API_KEY=your-random-secret

# ── Never-drop list (optional; not an env var) ───────────────────────────────
# waiver_plan never proposes dropping players you want to keep. Put them in
# data/derived/<season>/ml/squad_prefs.json (gitignored — never commit it):
#   {"never_drop": [{"player": "Examplename", "team": "ARS", "until_gw": 12,
#                    "note": "back from injury in GW10"}]}
# "player" is the FPL web_name; "team" the short club name; "code" (permanent
# player code) wins if given; "until_gw" and "note" are optional. Then `make derive`.

# ── Deadline checklist agent (optional; docs/DEADLINE_AGENT.md) ──────────────
# A compact checklist is delivered 30-60 min before each trades / waivers /
# lineup-lock deadline, but only while you are awake. All values below are the
# defaults; uncomment to change.

# Your IANA timezone. Awake hours are wall-clock in this zone (DST-aware).
# USER_TZ=America/New_York
# Awake window, HH:MM. AWAKE_END at or before AWAKE_START means "next day"
# (07:00-02:00 crosses midnight).
# AWAKE_START=07:00
# AWAKE_END=02:00
# Ideal delivery lead before the deadline, 30-60 minutes.
# CHECKLIST_LEAD_MIN=45
# Never deliver with less than this many minutes left to act (also the buffer
# before AWAKE_END).
# MIN_ACTION_MIN=15
# Research + derive start this long before delivery.
# RESEARCH_LEAD_MIN=25
# Optional phone push via ntfy. Topics are PUBLIC on ntfy.sh unless you
# self-host or protect them: use an unguessable name (openssl rand -hex 12)
# and never put league/entry ids or team names in it.
# NTFY_TOPIC=
# NTFY_SERVER=https://ntfy.sh
